{"causes": ["The flourishing intellectual environment of Nishapur provided fertile ground for scientific inquiry and scholarly exchange during the Islamic Golden Age.", "The extensive Greco-Arabic translation movement made classical Greek medical and philosophical texts accessible to scholars in the Islamic world.", "The patronage of various Islamic caliphates and regional dynasties fostered a culture of scientific research and medical innovation."], "effects": ["Al-Ilaqi's medical compendia became standard educational texts, disseminating advanced medical knowledge throughout madrasas in the Islamic world.", "His systematic approach to medical pedagogy influenced later physicians, including Ibn Sina, in their organization and presentation of medical science.", "His works contributed to the body of Islamic medical knowledge that would later be translated into Latin, impacting the development of European medicine."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "islamic-golden-age", "sourceName": "Islamic Golden Age", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "ali-ibn-yusuf-al-ilaqi", "targetName": "Ali ibn Yusuf al-Ilaqi", "context": "Ali ibn Yusuf al-Ilaqi's scholarly activities and innovations occurred during the intellectual zenith of the Islamic Golden Age (8th-13th centuries)."}, {"sourceSlug": "nishapur", "sourceName": "Nishapur", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "ali-ibn-yusuf-al-ilaqi", "targetName": "Ali ibn Yusuf al-Ilaqi", "context": "Ali ibn Yusuf al-Ilaqi was a prominent scholar and physician active in Nishapur, a major center of learning in Khurasan."}, {"sourceSlug": "greco-arabic-translation-movement", "sourceName": "Greco-Arabic Translation Movement", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "ali-ibn-yusuf-al-ilaqi", "targetName": "Ali ibn Yusuf al-Ilaqi", "context": "The availability of translated Greek medical texts through the Greco-Arabic Translation Movement profoundly influenced Ali ibn Yusuf al-Ilaqi's medical studies and commentaries."}, {"sourceSlug": "ali-ibn-yu